extraction_notes: "WB9 South America 2 printed 186-187 (cache p186-p187, page_offset 0). The class opens at the foot of printed 186; abilities and the stat block are printed 187, checked against a 110 dpi render, which agreed with the OCR on every number, including Rogue: Any (+6) printed without a percent sign. || XP: the Larhold Human Renegade / Plains ''Borg / ESP Specialist / Megaversal Trooper ladder on printed 192, as briefed. || GROUP: men-of-arms and men_of_arms true - a warrior O.C.C.; the book files its classes under the Larhold Barbarians section with no O.C.C. group heading. No sdc_base or mdc_base is printed. || RACE: human only - race_restrictions only none. The page is about humans raised among the tribes, although it opens with members of other races; the O.C.C. is titled Human Renegade and the abilities speak of human renegades. || ATTRIBUTES: minimum P.S., P.E. and P.P. 14. || BONUSES stored: +2D6x10 S.D.C. as a pool bonus, +3 P.S., +3 P.E., +2 P.P. || P.P.E. 6D6 plus P.E., +1D6 per level. || TRANSFORMATION: 25 P.P.E., three minutes per level. Its S.D.C.-to-M.D.C. conversion is TEMPORARY and leaves hit points out, so mdc_from_hp_sdc is NOT set - that flag is a permanent conversion of hit points and S.D.C. together, and this book''s Neo-Human decided the same for its temporary transformation. Stored as a special ability. P.P.E. is not tracked per use; the 1D4 M.D. plus P.S. bonus damage is prose. || SKILLS: Language: Larhold 98 (fixed; no literacy printed). Language one of choice +15 as a Language: Other pick. Basic Math is Mathematics: Basic 45+10. Riding: War Bison 50+15 = 65 at 4 per level. Wilderness Survival 30+12; Detect Ambush 30+8; Detect Concealment 25+10. W.P. Archery and Targeting as W.P. Archery; W.P. Sword; one W.P. of choice. Hand to Hand: Expert to Martial Arts or Assassin for one other skill each, no alignment condition printed. || RELATED: seven, plus two at level 3 and one at 6, 9 and 12. Communications +5; Domestic +10; Electrical Basic Electronics only; Espionage any; Mechanical Automotive Mechanics only; Medical Holistic Medicine only +5; Military any; Physical +5 where applicable; Pilot +5; Pilot Related any; Rogue +6 as printed (the percent sign is missing and the figure is stored as printed, not as the +5 the R.C.C. prints); Technical +10; W.P. any; Wilderness +10; Science none. SECONDARY: two each at levels 1, 3, 7 and 11, same limits without bonuses. || EQUIPMENT: composite bow as modern-bow (Spirit West''s modern compound bow; no plain composite bow row); 24 explosive arrows as a choice of the Triax explosive arrowheads. larhold-saber and larhold-hide-armor are this book''s rows (#1392); the saber row records the renegade''s unpowered 1D4 M.D. One energy weapon of choice, 1D4 E-clips and one modern weapon as catalog choices. The War Bison mount or small vehicle, the camping kit, dry rations and cooking utensils as on the Larhold Barbarian R.C.C. || MONEY: the Money line prints 2D6x100 in credit, stored, and 1D4x1000 in trade items, which is goods rather than coin and is recorded here. The Other Equipment line repeats the R.C.C.''s 1D6x1000 credits in cash or trade items; the Money line is taken as the authority and that figure is not stored. class-check warns that a race stating its own ppe_base or starting_money would discard these; race_restrictions only none means the class is never paired, so both always apply. Not supersedes_race. || Cybernetics: starts with none."
