## Lore

Not every Larhold was born one. The children and grandchildren of the tribes''
slaves sometimes claw their way to near-equal standing with their former
masters, and to be accepted they must prove themselves more vicious than the
Larhold themselves. Human renegades of this kind are brutal, cunning fighters
who use trickery to beat foes with supernatural strength, and few of them live
to see thirty.

A lifetime among transdimensional beings has left them flesh and blood but
charged with unusual mystic energy, which they can burn to briefly make
themselves as strong and tough as a true Larhold. A few turn on the tribes and
leave; they are hated by nearly everyone who has suffered at Larhold hands,
yet some have prospered, one rising to high command in New Babylon''s House of
War against the very tribes that raised him.
', 'published', 'data-script'
